  "full_text": "Mead\n\nIntroduction. Mead refers to items which can be consumed for temporary health and stamina boosts, as well as preventing harmful status effects.\nMead must first be crafted into a mead base at a Mead ketill and then fermented using a Fermenter.\nMead can be consumed with or without a Tankard, Dvergr tankard or a Horn of Celebration.\n\nCooldown. Meads have cooldown during which a player cannot drink another mead of the same type. Some meads share the same exclusion group:\n• Healing meads group: Minor healing mead Medium healing mead Major healing mead Lingering healing mead\n• Stamina meads group: Minor stamina mead Medium stamina mead Lingering stamina mead\n• Eitr meads group: Minor eitr mead Lingering eitr mead\n\nList of mead. As listed below, duration refers to the length of time over which the mead provides its effect, whereas cooldown is the length of time during which a player cannot drink another mead of the same type. Unless otherwise listed, each type of mead weighs 1.0 and stacks to 10.\n\nTrivia. • Before The Bog Witch update mead bases were crafted at the Cauldron.",
